          "To prevent the 28 parallel rings from splaying outward under traffic loads, Li Chun integrated interlocking lateral restraints: the deck tapers inward from 9.6 meters at the ends to 9.0 meters at the crown ('inward batter' generating self-locking lateral compression), adjacent voussoirs are pinned with iron dovetail cramps (yaotie) leaded into mortises, and five transverse iron tie-rods skewer all 28 rings into a unified elastic vault."
