          "At the sacred core of Hoi An's Fujian Hall and Cho Lon's Tue Thanh Hall sits Mazu, Empress of Heaven—historically rooted in Lin Moniang (960–987) of Meizhou Island, Putian, Fujian, elevated through imperial decrees from Lady and Celestial Consort to Empress of Heaven by Emperor Kangxi in 1684. Flanking her altar stand two nautical guardians: Thousand-Mile Eye (Qianliyan, green-faced, scanning distant storms) and Fair-Wind Ear (Shunfeng'er, red-faced, cupping his ear to wind shifts). Subsidiary altars honor Lady Kim Hoa (protector of childbirth), Dragon Mother (Guangdong river deity), the God of Wealth, and the Six Founding Clans who established Hoi An's Fujian Hall.",
